{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CevGoZzkguxeP17pARUGs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a complete understanding of the repository structure and conventions. Let me summarize my analysis:\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment model at `shipment/Shipment.kt:23-27` defines ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController at `shipment/ShipmentController.kt` handles create/read/list endpoints\n- InMemoryShipmentRepository at `shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt` provides persistence via ConcurrentHashMap\n- ApiException hierarchy at `api/ApiExceptions.kt` with ResourceNotFoundException and ConflictException\n- ErrorCode enum at `api/ApiError.kt:31-37` defines all machine-readable error codes\n- GlobalExceptionHandler at `api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt` converts exceptions to ApiError envelope with code/message/fields\n\n**Conventions in this repository:**\n1. Controllers throw ApiException subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409)\n2. All errors return consistent ApiError envelope: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\" } }`\n3. HTTP status codes follow REST standards (200, 201, 404, 409)\n4. Tests use MockMvc with assertions on both HTTP status AND error body structure (see OrderControllerTest lines 59-74)\n5. All tests reset repository state before each test with @BeforeEach\n6. No custom error handling in individual controllers; errors flow through GlobalExceptionHandler\n\n**Affected files (required changes):**\n1. `api/ApiError.kt` - Add new ErrorCode for status transition conflicts (needed for ConflictException to use a proper code)\n2. `shipment/ShipmentController.kt` - Add POST /{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint\n3. `shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Add 4 tests covering all scenarios (CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotent, CANCELLED rejection, 404)\n\n**Risks:**\n1. The in-memory repository and state transitions are not atomic; however this is pre-existing\n2. Must preserve all existing test passing behavior\n3. New error code must be semantically appropriate for the API contract\n\n**Open questions:** None - requirements and conventions are clear.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **`api/ApiError.kt`** (6 lines added):\n   - Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION` to the ErrorCode enum after existing shipment codes\n   - This represents the conflict when attempting to confirm a shipment that is not in CREATED or CONFIRMED status\n\n2. **`shipment/ShipmentController.kt`** (13 lines added):\n   - Add `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` method\n   - Retrieve shipment by ID; throw ResourceNotFoundException if not found\n   - Check shipment status:\n     - If CREATED: save and return shipment with CONFIRMED status\n     - If CONFIRMED: return as-is (idempotent, no save needed)\n     - If CANCELLED: throw ConflictException with the new error code\n   - Return the shipment (whether newly confirmed or already confirmed)\n\n3. **`shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt`** (40 lines added as 4 new test methods):\n   - `confirms a created shipment to CONFIRMED status` - verifies status transition and response\n   - `confirms an already confirmed shipment succeeds idempotently` - verifies retry safety\n   - `rejects confirm on a cancelled shipment with 409 conflict` - verifies error response with code\n   - `rejects confirm on unknown shipment with 404 not found` - verifies 404 with error code\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Could have reused `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` for the CANCELLED conflict case, but this is semantically wrong (the shipment doesn't \"already exist\" in that state—it exists in a conflicting state). The alternative risks confusing API clients and violates the \"consistent with the rest of this API\" criterion.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | HTTP Method | Path | Repository Read | Logic | Response | Errors |\n|------|-------------|------|-----------------|-------|----------|--------|\n| Happy path | POST | /shipments/S-1/confirm | findById(\"S-1\") | status==CREATED → save as CONFIRMED | 200 + shipment (CONFIRMED) | None |\n| Idempotent | POST | /shipments/S-2/confirm | findById(\"S-2\") | status==CONFIRMED → no-op | 200 + shipment (CONFIRMED) | None |\n| Conflict | POST | /shipments/S-3/confirm | findById(\"S-3\") | status==CANCELLED → throw | 409 + ApiError(code: SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION) | ConflictException |\n| Not found | POST | /shipments/missing/confirm | findById(\"missing\")→null | throw | 404 + ApiError(code: SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND) | ResourceNotFoundException |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **Test: confirm CREATED → CONFIRMED** \n   - Create shipment (status=CREATED)\n   - POST /shipments/{id}/confirm\n   - Assert status 200, response has status=\"CONFIRMED\"\n\n2. **Test: confirm CONFIRMED (idempotent)**\n   - Create shipment (status=CREATED)\n   - POST /shipments/{id}/confirm (first call)\n   - POST /shipments/{id}/confirm (second call - the retry)\n   - Assert status 200 both times, status=\"CONFIRMED\" both times\n\n3. **Test: confirm CANCELLED → 409**\n   - Create shipment, then manually save with status=CANCELLED (via repository direct write)\n   - POST /shipments/{id}/confirm\n   - Assert status 409, error.code=\"SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION\"\n\n4. **Test: confirm non-existent → 404**\n   - POST /shipments/nonexistent/confirm\n   - Assert status 404, error.code=\"SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\"\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3425,"cache_read_input_tokens":17186,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3425},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":nu