rect: represents attempting to confirm a shipment in an invalid state\n   - Necessary change for the API contract\n\n2. **`shipment/ShipmentController.kt`** (21 lines added):\n   - Added `confirm()` method with @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   - Properly handles all three status cases using when expression\n   - Returns persisted shipment for CREATED→CONFIRMED\n   - Returns unchanged shipment for CONFIRMED (idempotent)\n   - Throws ConflictException with new error code for CANCELLED\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException (existing pattern) for missing shipment\n   - Updated class docstring to reflect new feature\n   - No changes to existing methods\n\n3. **`shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt`** (40 lines added):\n   - Four new test methods covering all requirement cases\n   - Follow existing test patterns (MockMvc, assertions on status and body)\n   - Properly reset state between tests\n   - Test cancelled shipment by writing directly to repository (same pattern as ShipmentStatus.CANCELLED comment in Shipment.kt)\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All requirements implemented and verified.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint that transitions CREATED \n              shipments to CONFIRMED with idempotent retry support, rejecting CANCELLED \n              shipments with 409 and missing shipments with 404.\n\nChanged       api/ApiError.kt — added SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE_TRANSITION error code \n              (necessary for ConflictException to express state validation failure)\n              \n              shipment/ShipmentController.kt — added confirm() endpoint with state \n              transition logic and error handling consistent with existing endpoints\n              \n              shipment/ShipmentControllerTest.kt — added 4 test methods covering \n              CREATED→CONFIRMED, idempotent retry, CANCELLED rejection, and 404 cases\n\nTests         1. confirms a created shipment to CONFIRMED status — verifies successful \n                 transition from CREATED to CONFIRMED with 200 response\n              2. confirms an already confirmed shipment succeeds idempotently — verifies \n                 retry safety and idempotent behavior (no state change)\n              3. rejects confirm on a cancelled shipment with 409 conflict — verifies \n                 proper error code and HTTP 409 status\n              4. rejects confirm on unknown shipment with 404 not found — verifies \n                 ResourceNotFoundException and proper error envelope\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test (from sample-service/)\n              Result: BUILD SUCCESS - 17 tests, 0 failures\n              Details: 4 order tests, 1 app test, 9 shipment tests (5 existing + 4 new), \n                       3 customer tests all passing\n\nNot done      Nothing — all requirements implemented, tested, and verified.\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3340,"cache_read_input_tokens":25946,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3340},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f4c8499c-e47d-48ea-86fe-11b73d2de2b8","uuid":"ca1c4e27-15ec-43a7-ae9e-edefc0311066","timestamp":"2026-09-10T19:00:50.459Z","request_id":"req_011CevGsWUn4hKh7mft5jTt9"}
